1
00:00:00,383 --> 00:00:02,383
(Leonard:)See, this right here,
what you're doing,

2
00:00:02,385 --> 00:00:05,225
(Leonard:)can you please not do that
around Sheldon's mom?

3
00:00:05,222 --> 00:00:08,592
(Dr Hofstadter:)Why? Are you attracted
to her, too?

4
00:00:08,592 --> 00:00:10,192
(Sheldon:)Of course not.

5
00:00:10,193 --> 00:00:13,023
She's-she's just a very
sweet and God-fearing lady,

6
00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:15,199
(Leonard:)and you have to be
respectful of her beliefs.

7
00:00:15,198 --> 00:00:16,598
(Dr Hofstadter:)Leonard, I'm an adult.

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,030
(Dr Hofstadter:)I know how to conduct myself
around people

9
00:00:19,035 --> 00:00:20,835
(Dr Hofstadter:)from different
walks of life.

10
00:00:20,837 --> 00:00:21,837
(Sheldon:)Thank you.

11
00:00:21,838 --> 00:00:22,838
(Dr Hofstadter:)Where is she from again?

12
00:00:22,839 --> 00:00:25,239
(Leonard:)East Texas.
Ugh.

13
00:00:29,078 --> 00:00:30,608
(Leonard:)Hey, look who's here.

14
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:34,584
Oh, Dr. Hofstadter,
it's so good to see you again.

15
00:00:34,584 --> 00:00:35,784
(Dr Hofstadter:)Likewise.

16
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:38,355
I read your paper;
it was very impressive.

17
00:00:38,355 --> 00:00:39,225
(Sheldon:)Oh, thank you.

18
00:00:39,222 --> 00:00:41,222
(Leonard:)We just spent
two hours in traffic.

19
00:00:41,224 --> 00:00:44,464
(Leonard:)Did you think to mention to me
that you liked our paper?

20
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,891
(Dr Hofstadter:)Of course I did, but
it's a mother's job

21
00:00:46,896 --> 00:00:49,466
(Dr Hofstadter:)to make sure her child's
self-esteem is not dependent

22
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:50,666
(Dr Hofstadter:)on anyone's approval.

23
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:55,305
(Leonard:)That's so sweet,
you think I have self-esteem.

24
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:59,245
Dr. Hofstadter, I want you
to meet my mother, Mary.

